  "notes": [
    "This is a full self-contained calendar-year 2026 cycle (January 4 through December 27), plus a January 3, 2027 entry confirming the cycle repeats annually (it names the exact same two parishes -- St. Alban's, Bay City and St. Christopher's, Grand Blanc -- as March 29, 2026) -- that January 2027 entry is excluded here as out of calendar-2026 range, not fabricated or force-included.",
    "The source's own standing preamble ('EVERY WEEK PRAY FOR: Presiding Bishop... Bishop Anne Hodges-Copple... partner dioceses and their bishops... ELCA synod bishop', plus a list of postulants/candidates for Holy Orders and Deacons, and retired clergy generally) is a fixed weekly constant, not tied to any one date -- deliberately excluded from `entries` (which hold only the week-keyed rotation) and disclosed here in full rather than repeated into every single week: 'Presiding Bishop, Sean Rowe; Bishop Anne Hodges-Copple our Assisting Bishop, the Standing Committee of the Diocese of the Great Lakes; for our partner dioceses and their bishops, Bonnie Perry, Bishop of Michigan; Rayford Ray, Bishop of Northern Michigan; Dame Sarah Mullally, Archbishop of Canterbury; Stephen Cottrell, Archbishop of York; Julie Schneider-Thomas Bishop of the North/West Lower Michigan Synod of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA). We pray for all those in our diocese discerning calls to ministry, both lay and ordained. In particular, we pray for those in our dioceses preparing for the Sacred Order of Priests, including Abraham Anei, Laurie Atwater, Bryan Boughton, Thon Deng, Rebekah Taylor, and Janet Huff-Worvie. We pray also for those in our dioceses preparing for the Sacred Order of Deacons, including Chris Hamel, Kathryn Hawkins, Laura Hoekstra, Gerry Stackhouse, Paige Faith Wilson. We remember with gratitude the retired clergy of the diocese.' Matches this corpus's existing precedent for a standing preamble (see episcopal-arkansas.json's own 'Pray daily for' disclosure).",
    "Each parish subject's `note` field holds the specific clergy/warden name and title the source prints alongside that congregation that week -- this is the source's own per-week content (who currently leads or represents that parish), not an editorial annotation, but `note` is the schema field that fits since `subjectShape` has no dedicated clergy-attribution field.",
    "'Emmaus Monastery, Vestaburg' (April 12) and 'St. Gregory's Abbey, Three Rivers' (May 24) are religious communities, not parishes, and are recorded as `category` subjects (full text including the resident/associated names) rather than `parish` subjects.",
    "'DeAnne Swiercz, Senior Wanden' (February 1) is preserved exactly as printed, per this corpus's standing rule against silently correcting apparent typos (likely 'Senior Warden').",
    "July 19's 'St. Peter's-by-the-Lake, Montague' is the only parish entry with no clergy/warden name given in the source -- its `note` field is correspondingly absent, not fabricated."
  ],
